WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.925
Here's Microsoft's starting point.

2
00:00:01.925 --> 00:00:05.742
Learn's review page has a PowerShell
script that finds one app,

3
00:00:05.742 --> 00:00:09.484
removes all of its delegated
grants, then tries to remove all

4
00:00:09.484 --> 00:00:13.600
of its application permissions,
plus the matching Graph requests.

5
00:00:13.600 --> 00:00:16.742
A separate tutorial shows
how to grant and revoke,

6
00:00:16.742 --> 00:00:20.038
which the second lab uses
to restore what it removes.

7
00:00:20.038 --> 00:00:22.706
As in earlier chapters, the page is pinned

8
00:00:22.706 --> 00:00:26.001
unmodified with checked
hashes and a weekly watch.

9
00:00:26.001 --> 00:00:29.575
The harness then runs the
script exactly as published,

10
00:00:29.575 --> 00:00:33.150
against stand-ins that follow
Learn's own API contract.

11
00:00:33.150 --> 00:00:35.710
That contract is where
things get interesting.
